# test/mutations.list — F6 named-mutation registry (tier-2 surface)
#
# One mutation per line. A mutation "targets" a check when a seeded
# container run against the mutated tree no longer produces that
# check's expected finding, i.e. its check_id flips out of the audit
# output (or the seeded tier-2 driver fails on a probe for it).
#
# FORMAT — three tab-separated fields per entry line:
#
#   check_id <TAB> target <TAB> sed_expression
#
#   check_id        The check_id whose expected finding should flip
#                   out of the --json findings[] after the mutation.
#   target          Repo-relative path of the file the sed applies to
#                   (the driver applies it to a scratch copy of the
#                   tree and restores with git after each entry).
#   sed_expression  A single sed s-command, e.g.
#                   s|json_push alert security.fail2ban_banned security |json_push alert security.fail2ban_bannedX security |
#
# CONVENTIONS
#   - Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#   - The sed uses '|' as the delimiter so the regex slashes (e.g.
#     /usr/bin/find) stay literal; no expression here needs '/'.
#   - Fields are applied verbatim by the driver with no shell
#     expansion: sed -i "<sed_expression>" "<target>".
#   - Dots in search strings are plain-text identifiers and match
#     'any char' in regex; that is harmless here because every
#     search string occurs on exactly one line of its target file
#     (verified at registry creation — keep it that way when adding
#     entries).
#   - Each entry must be a single line: no tabs, no backslash
#     line-continuations inside a field.
#   - Family A entries mutate the seeded STATE (seed.sh); family B
#     entries mutate the audit's own emission (scripts/box-audit.sh)
#     by renaming the check_id it pushes. Both families flip the
#     targeted check_id out of the output; family B is the only
#     family available for checks whose seed state is produced
#     post-boot by test/install-seeded.sh (sockets, bans, journal
#     lines) — those lines live in the driver, which the registry
#     must not edit.
#
# COVERAGE — one entry per check_id test/install-seeded.sh asserts
# (the nine listed below plus the F2 jail and the #38 counts field,
# eleven total):
#   security.outbound_remote_count, security.outbound_remote_count_v6,
#   security.suid_delta, security.fail2ban_banned,
#   security.fail2ban_jail, updates.security_delta,
#   updates.security_pending, system.failed_units,
#   system.cron_d_dropins, security.new_port
#
# CHECKS THAT CANNOT BE BROKEN BY A SINGLE SED: none. Every listed
# check_id has a single-line sed that flips it (above). Noted for
# completeness: the v4/v6 outbound *socket seeding* and the fail2ban
# banip calls are multi-line driver actions and cannot be removed by
# one sed — but each of those checks also has a one-line emission
# site in scripts/box-audit.sh, which is what these entries target.
#
# The driver (test/mutation-coverage.sh, separate card) reads this
# file, applies each entry to a scratch tree, re-runs the seeded
# tier-2 suite, and records FLIPPED (caught — good) or SURVIVED
# (uncovered surface — signal) per entry.

security.fail2ban_banned	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push alert security.fail2ban_banned security |json_push alert security.fail2ban_bannedX security |
security.fail2ban_jail	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push alert security.fail2ban_jail security |json_push alert security.fail2ban_jailX security |
security.new_port	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.new_port security |json_push warn security.new_portX security |
security.outbound_remote_count	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.outbound_remote_count security |json_push warn security.outbound_remote_countX security |
security.outbound_remote_count_v6	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.outbound_remote_count_v6 security |json_push warn security.outbound_remote_count_v6X security |
security.suid_delta	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.suid_delta security |json_push warn security.suid_deltaX security |
updates.security_delta	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn updates.security_delta updates |json_push warn updates.security_deltaX updates |
updates.security_pending	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn updates.security_pending updates |json_push warn updates.security_pendingX updates |
system.failed_units	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn system.failed_units system |json_push warn system.failed_unitsX system |
system.cron_d_dropins	test/install-docker/seeded/seed.sh	s|^printf .fake-cron-line|: # F6-registry mutation removes the cron.d drop-in (family A)|
security.ssh_fails	scripts/box-audit.sh	s|json_push warn security.ssh_fails security |json_push warn security.ssh_failsX security |
